  "exact_bilingual_statement": "# 00000005960\n\n**English.** Definition: The spectrum and the eigenvector statistics are two layers. Conjecture: There exist two ensembles with the same eigenvalue spectrum but different eigenvector statistics, and the separation is realized by an explicit free parametrization with the same spectrum but different orientation. (same spectrum-different vector orientation separation)\n\n**中文。** 定义：谱与特征向量统计指两层。猜想：存在两系综的特征值谱相同而特征向量统计不同,分离由同谱异定向的显式自由参数化实现。（谱同-向量统计异定向分离）\n",
  "source_scope_notes": "English and Chinese agree on an existential assertion: two ensembles with the same eigenvalue spectrum, different eigenvector statistics, and an explicit free parametrization preserving the spectrum while changing orientation. No dimension, Gaussianity or regularity restriction is stated. A faithful construction should specify genuine ensemble probability laws, the meaning of equal spectra, an explicit parameter family, and a sign/phase-independent eigenvector statistic; merely changing an eigenvector sign would not establish an intrinsic orientation/statistical distinction. Mathematical/formal correctness is a separate review.",
